TEST 38475 -- ATMF - recover from USB drive
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-24 (lab date; device clocks 2026-09-23 19:45-21:12 UTC), tb470
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20 on the DUT and the master
DUT:    IE520-sa -- standalone IE520 (S/N 264A23068, /dev/u3), stack ID 1 (port1.0.x),
        AMF MEMBER. 28.9 GB USB stick in the DUT.
Master: IE520-stk (3-member stack, master = member 3), AMF master of network "tb470",
        backup media = USB stick in member 3; `atmf recovery-server` enabled.
Other:  4050-5g (member, over sa1), x230-10GP (member, over sa2).
Case precondition: "DUT requires virtual-link for this test"

VERDICT: PASS -- all four steps. The DUT recovered from its USB recovery file, rejoined
         over its virtual link, pulled its files from the master and came back with a
         running-config IDENTICAL to the pre-wipe baseline.
         (Replaces run 1, 2026-09-23: FAIL at step 4, confounded -- see PRECONDITION.)

